PMID,QID,Question,Answer,Evidence,Rationale
40391923,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","Of the 488 samples (420 plasma, 68 DBS samples), 234 (48%) had a VL >1000 copies/mL and underwent sequencing. IN sequencing was successful for 227 of 234 participants (97.0%) and PR/RT sequencing was successful for 217 of the 227 with IN sequences (95.6%).",The paper explicitly states that samples were collected from patients and that sequencing was performed on these samples.
40391923,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","The study involves prospective enrollment from routine clinical care at sites in Asia, South America, and sub-Saharan Africa selected to represent diverse settings, programmatic contexts, and non-B HIV subtypes. Enrollment began in June 2022 and will continue until May 2025. Further details are outlined in the study protocol. In brief, the study includes adults and adolescents (aged 10-19 years) with at least 1 routine viral load (VL) >1000 copies/mL while on DTG-based ART. Plasma or dried blood spots (DBS) are collected depending on local storage capacities. Samples are sent to centralized laboratories, and genotypic resistance testing is performed on those with VL >1000 copies/mL.",The paper focuses on genotypic resistance testing rather than in vitro drug susceptibility.
40391923,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,"The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are PV008448-PV008641, PV407014-PV407203, and PV419497-PV419583.","The sequences have been uploaded to GenBank under accession numbers PV008448-PV008641, PV407014-PV407203, and PV419497-PV419583.",The paper explicitly lists the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced isolates.
40391923,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The HIV genes reported to have been sequenced are the integrase (IN) and protease/reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) regions.,Sanger sequencing of integrase (IN) and protease/reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) regions was conducted using the ThermoFisher HIV-1 Genotyping Kit.,The paper specifies that these regions were sequenced.
40391923,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from Cameroon, Côte d'Ivoire, Malawi, Republic of Congo, Uganda, Zambia, and Zimbabwe.","Here, we present data from participants enrolled between June 2022 and December 2024 at 16 study sites in 7 African countries: Cameroon (n = 2), Côte d'Ivoire (n = 2), Malawi (n = 2), Republic of Congo (n = 2), Uganda (n = 2), Zambia (n = 5), and Zimbabwe (n = 1).",The paper lists the countries from which the samples were obtained.
40391923,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained between June 2022 and December 2024.,"Here, we present data from participants enrolled between June 2022 and December 2024 at 16 study sites in 7 African countries.",The paper provides the time frame for sample collection.
40391923,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The method used for sequencing was Sanger sequencing.,Sanger sequencing of integrase (IN) and protease/reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) regions was conducted using the ThermoFisher HIV-1 Genotyping Kit.,The paper specifies that Sanger sequencing was used.
40391923,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","Sanger sequencing of integrase (IN) and protease/reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) regions was conducted using the ThermoFisher HIV-1 Genotyping Kit. Sequences were analyzed with the Stanford HIVdb algorithm V9.8. Sequences were analyzed with the Stanford HIVdb algorithm V9.8, and HIV subtypes were determined using COMET and Rega V3.46.89. Plasma or dried blood spots (DBS) are collected depending on local storage capacities. Samples are sent to centralized laboratories, and genotypic resistance testing is performed on those with VL >1000 copies/ml.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples.
40391923,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The types of samples sequenced were plasma and dried blood spots (DBS).,"Of the 488 samples (420 plasma, 68 DBS samples), 234 (48%) had a VL >1000 copies/mL and underwent sequencing.",The paper specifies that both plasma and DBS were used for sequencing.
40391923,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","We report the proportion of individuals with resistance among those with documented viremia (VL >1000 copies/mL) on DTG-based ART, along with the associated mutational patterns. Most (n = 415, 85%) had 2 or more consecutive VL measurements >1000 copies/mL before enrollment.",The paper mentions that samples were obtained from individuals experiencing virological failure.
40391923,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients were not in a clinical trial; the study was conducted as a routine clinical care analysis.","The study involves prospective enrollment from routine clinical care at sites in Asia, South America, and sub-Saharan Africa selected to represent diverse settings, programmatic contexts, and non-B HIV subtypes.",The paper describes the study as focusing on routine clinical care rather than a clinical trial.
40391923,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,234 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"Of the 488 samples (420 plasma, 68 DBS samples), 234 (48%) had a VL >1000 copies/mL and underwent sequencing.",The paper states that 234 samples underwent sequencing.
40391923,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","Most (n = 421, 85%) had 2 or more consecutive VL measurements >1000 copies/mL before enrollment. We report the proportion of individuals with resistance among those with documented viremia (VL >1000 copies/mL) on DTG-based ART, along with the associated mutational patterns. Most participants (n = 421, 86.3%) had prior exposure to at least 1 ART regimen, while 67 (13.7%) were treatment-naive when they started DTG.","The paper mentions that most participants had prior exposure to ARV drugs, specifically mentioning DTG-based ART, and had experienced virological failure on the regimen."
40391923,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The drug classes received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing include NRTIs, integrase inhibitors (INSTIs), and PIs.","Most (n = 447, 91.6%) were on a regimen that contained DTG with 2 Nucleos(t)ide Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors (NRTIs), with 336 of 447 (75.2%) receiving tenofovir/lamivudine/dolutegravir (TLD). Previous exposure to raltegravir was rare (n = 9, 1.8%). Protease inhibitor (PI) resistance was rare. Major PI DRMs were detected in 8 of 57 (14.0%) participants with major INSTI DRMs. All participants with PI DRMs had predicted susceptibility to darunavir.","The paper mentions exposure to NRTIs, INSTIs, and PIs, as well as specific drugs in these classes."
40391923,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The drugs received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing included dolutegravir (DTG), tenofovir, lamivudine, raltegravir, and darunavir.","Most (n = 447, 91.6%) were on a regimen that contained DTG with 2 Nucleos(t)ide Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors (NRTIs), with 336 of 447 (75.2%) receiving tenofovir/lamivudine/dolutegravir (TLD). Previous exposure to raltegravir was rare (n = 9, 1.8%). Protease inhibitor (PI) resistance was rare. Major PI DRMs were detected in 8 of 57 (14.0%) participants with major INSTI DRMs. All participants with PI DRMs had predicted susceptibility to darunavir.",The paper specifies that these drugs were received by individuals before sequencing.
40391923,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the sequences from the paper were made publicly available.","The sequences have been uploaded to GenBank under accession numbers PV008448-PV008641, PV407014-PV407203, and PV419497-PV419583.",The paper explicitly states that the sequences were made publicly available through GenBank.
