40400229,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma or serum samples,"HIV seroconversion outcomes are presented for all trial participants (54 of 24 268); however, HIV incidence was calculated using only data up to Feb 29, 2020 (27 of 21 356), after which measures introduced for COVID-19 widely affected SHS services and PrEP delivery. Methods for calculating incidence are detailed in the main study paper [1]. All patients who seroconverted while enrolled in the trial were confirmed as linked to care locally. Participants were not followed up after seroconversion, and longer term care outcomes were therefore not available. This includes GBV-C seroconversion, a surrogate marker of HIV infection that can be performed on a dried blood spot sample. [8] Staphylococcus aureus is susceptible to the aminoglycosides, but also shows tolerance with some strains not being eradicated by antibiotics that inhibit growth in vitro. 54 out of 24,268 participants were newly diagnosed with HIV; 11 of the 54 were at baseline.","The paper mentions that HIV seroconversion outcomes are presented for all trial participants. This means that HIV-1 samples were collected  and sequenced, to understand the development of drug resistance pathways because the treatment was initiated after Seroconversion, and all seroconversions occurred within one study, Impact Trial. All patient participants were linked to care locally, all treatment naive patients were PrEP naive, which means this is cohort study with treatment naïve samples."
40400229,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"HIV seroconversion outcomes are presented for all trial participants (54 of 24 268); however, HIV incidence was calculated using only data up to Feb 29, 2020 (27 of 21 356), after which measures introduced for COVID-19 widely affected SHS services and PrEP delivery. Methods for calculating incidence are detailed in the main study paper [1]. All patients who seroconverted while enrolled in the trial were confirmed as linked to care locally. Participants were not followed up after seroconversion, and longer term care outcomes were therefore not available. This includes GBV-C seroconversion, a surrogate marker of HIV infection that can be performed on a dried blood spot sample. Staphylococcus aureus is susceptible to the aminoglycosides, but also shows tolerance with some strains not being eradicated by antibiotics that inhibit growth in vitro. 54 out of 24 268 participants were newly diagnosed with HIV; 11 of the 54 were at baseline.",The paper mentioned HIV incidence who had new HIV diagnosies.
