40713598,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI","All participants (100%) had at least one DRM; 100% NNRTIs, 75% NRTIs (Fig. 1A & B). M184I/V (N = 15) and NNRTI-associated K103N (N = 12) were the most common DRMs.","The paper mentions the presence of mutations associated with NRTI (Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor) and NNRTI (Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor) resistance, indicating that individuals had received drugs from these classes."
40713598,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Abacavir, lamivudine, nevirapine, efavirenz, zidovudine",Details of regimen at the time of virological failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy; Dolutegravir-based ART following its introduction and a change in HIV treatment guidelines in Ghana,"The drugs received by individuals included Abacavir (ABC), Lamivudine (3TC), Nevirapine (NVP), Efavirenz (EFV), and Zidovudine (ZDV). All these drugs were NRTI or NNRTI class drugs."
