40763144,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper does report HIV sequences from patient samples.","HIVDR was defined as having at least one mutation with a penalty score of  9;15 if the sample collection year was between 1st January 2021 30th December 2023 abstract We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the WestNile region of Uganda; Methods We conducted a retrospective crosssectional analysis of HIVDR data in the WestNile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive Anti retroviral therapy ART services All PLHIV regardless of age who had been on ART for at least oneyear experienced virological failure and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021 30th December 2023 were included in the study Demographic and clinical data were extracted from the National HIVDR database HIVDR was defined as having at least one mutation with a penalty score of >= 15","The paper mentions that HIVDR was defined as having at least one mutation with a penalty score of >= 15, and demographic and clinical data were extracted from the National HIVDR database, which contains HIV sequences from patient samples after undergoing HIVDR test showing the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples."
40763144,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) poses a challenge to managing people living with HIV (PLHIV), particularly among those experiencing virological failure (VF). The West-Nile region of Uganda faces HIV treatment challenges and has a high virological failure rate. We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda. Methods We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional analysis of HIVDR data in the West-Nile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive Anti-retroviral therapy (ART) services. All PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one-year, experienced virological failure and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023 were included in the study. Demographic and clinical data were extracted from the National HIVDR database. HIVDR was defined as having at least one mutation with a penalty score of ≥ 15. PLHIV were characterized based on age, gender and clinical history. Logistic regression models determined factors associated with HIVDR with a p-value of < 0.05 considered significant; Results A total 295 records were analyzed Of these majority were female 56 6 and adults aged 20 years 49 2 The median age was 19 Inter quartile range [IQR 13-41] years and median duration on ART was 8 IQR 5-10 years Overall 218 73 9 had HIVDR with 66 of subjects having Non nucleoside reverse transcriptase NNRTI mutations M184V I 50 K103N 34 and TAMS 26 were the commonest mutations Resistance to Etravirine 27 was higher than that of Dolutegravir 12 and Darunavir 5 After accounting for gender age Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor NRTI anchor drug ART regimen type and World Health Organization WHO clinical stage of the participants long duration on ART aOR 1 15 95 CI 1 05-1 26 p 0 003 adolescents failing on first line aOR 3 80 95 CI 1 02-14 08 p 0 046 and participants failing on 2nd line aOR 3 64 95 CI 1 18-11 21 p 0 024 as indications for the HIVDR test and the year of HIVDR sample collection aOR 0 21 95 CI 0 07-0 69 p 0 010 were independently associated with HIVDR mutations","The paper focuses on HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) mutations and their prevalence among individuals with virological failure. It does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or data, indicating that such data is not reported."
40763144,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,"Prevalence of HIV drug resistance its correlates and common mutations among people living with HIV failing on ART in northern Uganda A crosssectional study Prevalence of HIV drug resistance its correlates and common mutations among people living with HIV failing on ART in northern Uganda method We conducted a retrospective crosssectional analysis of HIVDR data in the WestNile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive Anti retroviral therapy ART services All PLHIV regardless of age who had been on ART for at least oneyear experienced virological failure and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 20211st December 2023 were included in the study.,","The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers, indicating that they were not provided. This information is typically included in the Methods or Results sections of a paper, but it is absent here."
40763144,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper reports sequencing of the NRTI, NNRTI, INSTI, and PI genes.","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) poses a challenge to managing people living with HIV (PLHIV), particularly among those experiencing virological failure (VF). The West-Nile region of Uganda faces HIV treatment challenges and has a high virological failure rate. We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda; By using un luteal coupling multiplex peptide nucleic acid PCR clamp coupled with Sanger sequencing for genotyping of the RT  IN and PR regions Abstract Background HIV drug resistance HIVDR poses a challenge to managing people living with HIV PLHIV particularly among those experiencing virological failure VF The WestNile region of Uganda faces HIV treatment challenges and has a high virological failure rate We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluate","The paper mentions that sequencing is performed to identify mutations in the NRTI, NNRTI, INSTI, and PI genes, indicating that these genes were reported to have been sequenced."
40763144,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Uganda.,"We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional study in the West-Nile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive ART services. All PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, had a non-suppressed HIV viral load (>1000 copies/ml) and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023.","The study was conducted in the West-Nile region of Uganda, and all the samples were collected from health facilities within this region, indicating that Uganda is the only country from which the sequenced samples were obtained."
40763144,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from the years 2021 to 2023.,"All PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, had a non-suppressed HIV viral load (>1000 copies/ml) and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023.","The paper specifies that the HIVDR tests were conducted between 1st January 2021 and 30th December 2023, indicating that the sequenced samples were obtained during these years."
40763144,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The method used for sequencing was not specified in the paper.,A Plasma or dried blood spot (DBS) sample is collected and referred to the HIVDR testing facility at a central national laboratory Here RNA extraction is done using commercial kits followed by reverse transcription and Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) amplification PCR is a molecular technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences by generating millions of copies from a small initial sample This step is crucial for increasing the quantity of genetic material required for sequencing sequencing where individual mutations are identified using either Sanger sequencing or Next generation sequencing is then carried out Mutations are identified and interpreted using the Stanford HIV drug resistance database If the 1st January 2024 is considered the serviceBaseline participant characteristics and HIVDR Of the 295 participants 167 56 6 were female and the median age was 19 years Inter quartile range IQR 13 41 The participants had been on ART for a median 8 years IQR 5 10 and 59 3 were on INSTIs at sample collection,The paper mentioned that sequencing is carried out using either Sanger sequencing. This indicates that Sanger sequencing was one of the methods used for sequencing the samples.
40763144,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) poses a challenge to managing people living with HIV (PLHIV), particularly among those experiencing virological failure (VF). The West-Nile region of Uganda faces HIV treatment challenges and has a high virological failure rate We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluate Participants included all PLHIV regardless of age who having been on ART for at least oneyear experienced virological failure underwent HIVDR test between 1st January 20211st December 2023 We conducted a retrospective crosssectional study In total 295 records were analyzed 81 3 had HIVDR results 218 73 9 had HIVDR 66 of subjects had NNRTI mutations Method Previously described methodologies for HIVDR testing [17 19] were adopted All PLHIV on ART in Uganda receive a VL test annually Those with a non suppressed VL undergo intensive adherence counselling IAC for three months with a repeat VL at the end Individuals with a persistent non suppressed VL are eligible for an HIVDR test Plasma or dried blood spot DBS sample is collected and referred to the HIVDR testing facility at a central national laboratory Here RNA extraction is done using commercial kits followed by reverse transcription and Polymerase Chain Reaction PCR amplification PCR is a molecular technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences by generating millions of copies from a small initial sample This step is crucial for increasing the quantity of genetic material required for sequencing sequencing where individual mutations are identified using either Sanger sequencing or Next generation sequencing is then carried out Mutations are identified and interpreted using the Stanford HIV drug resistance database.","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, indicating that this step was not performed."
40763144,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma and dried blood spot (DBS) samples were sequenced.,A Plasma or dried blood spot (DBS) sample is collected and referred to the HIVDR testing facility at a central national laboratory Here RNA extraction is done using commercial kits followed by reverse transcription and Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) amplification,"The paper specifies that either plasma or dried blood spot (DBS) samples were collected for sequencing, indicating the type of clinical specimens used."
40763144,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.",All PLHIV regardless of age who had been on ART for at least one year had a non suppressed HIV viral load gt 1000 copies ml and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021 30th December 2023,"The paper included PLHIV who had experienced virological failure and had undergone an HIVDR test, indicating that sequences were obtained from these individuals."
40763144,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients in the study were not in a clinical trial.","We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional analysis of HIVDR data in the West-Nile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive Anti-retroviral therapy (ART) services. All PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one-year, experienced virological failure and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023 were included in the study. All PLHIV on ART in Uganda receive a VL test annually. Those with a non suppressed VL undergo intensive adherence counselling (IAC) for three months with a repeat VL at the end Individuals with a persistent non suppressed VL are eligible for an HIVDR test A Plasma or dried blood spot DBS sample is collected and referred to the HIVDR testing facility at a central national laboratory Here RNA extraction is done using commercial kits followed by reverse transcription and Polymerase Chain Reaction PCR amplification.","The paper mentions the study is a retrospective cross-sectional study, and  all the samples were collected from health facilities within Uganda, No clinical trial was mentioned."
