41088231,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide. Specimen 230794was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China.","The paper states that the individual was  identified from a drug resistance surveillance among 5602 ART-naïve individuals in 2023, indicating the individual had not received ARV drugs."
