41091504,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No sequences from patient samples are reported in the paper, the study focuses on HIV-1 protease mutants and darunavir binding studies.","The study we are using a very potent inhibitor, darunavir, bound to a series of 28 variants of HIV-1 protease with affinities from picomolar to micromolar, to develop an accurate method for predicting resistance.",The paper focuses on the molecular dynamics simulations and machine learning modeling of HIV-1 protease variants and does not mention any patient-derived sequences.
41091504,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"The paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data, it focuses on molecular dynamics simulations and machine learning modeling of HIV-1 protease variants.",To develop an accurate method for predicting resistance. Our optimized strategy involves rerefining cocryystal structures to ensure accurate inhibitor geometries and combining parallel molecular dynamics simulations with feature selection to develop a robust machine learning model to predict loss of potency and resistance.,The paper describes the use of darunavir in the context of resistance predictions but does not mention any experimental data on drug susceptibility.
