41130593,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Next-generation sequencing (MiSeq; Illumina),"Genotypic CA resistance testing at Monogram was conducted using a next-generation sequencing platform (MiSeq; Illumina), which is a validated test run in a Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments-certified laboratory.","The paper describes the use of next-generation sequencing (MiSeq; Illumina) for genotypic resistance testing, indicating the method used for sequencing."
41130593,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"HIV-1 single-copy assay (SCA) testing was performed retrospectively on the Hologic Panther platform using a multiple replicate strategy (Accelevir Diagnostics, Baltimore, Maryland) on samples from EAP participants in the LEN group who acquired HIV-1 [18,19].","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, indicating that this was not done."
